## CONVERSATION

<USER_REQUEST>
If the loading dose of phenytoin in children is 20 mg/kg of body weight to be infused at a rate of 0.5 mg/kg/min, over how many minutes should the dose be administered to a 32-lb. child?
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
To calculate the time it takes to deliver the loading dose, follow these steps:

1. **Convert the body mass from pounds to kilograms**:  
   \( 32 \text{ lb} \times 0.454 \text{ kg/lb} = 14.4 \text{ kg} \).  
2. **Calculate the total loading dose**:  
   \( 14.4 \text{ kg} \times 20 \text{ mg/kg} = 288 \text{ mg} \).  
3. **Calculate the time to inflate the delivery**:  
   \( \frac{288 \text{ mg}}{0.5 \text{ mg/min}} = 576 \text{ min} \).  

The delivery time is \(\boxed{576 \text{ minutes}}\).
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

