1. Temperature-based smart materials: These materials can be tuned to respond to temperature changes in the form of changes in their color, color-responsability, or mechanical properties. By modifying the polymer's composition, the transition temperature can be altered. By incorporating stimuli-active materials, such as shape-changing polymers, the material's ability to respond to temperature can be improved.

2. Polymer-based smart materials that respond to pH: These materials can be tailored to improve their color-responsifying properties. By modifying the choice of the active material, the color-responsifying properties can be improved.

