\[
F = qE
\]  
Substituting \(q = 1.60 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{C}\) and \(E = 500 \, \text{N/C}\):  
\[
F = (1.60 \times 10^{-19}) \times (500) = 800 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{N}
\]  
Now, substitute \(F\) into the acceleration formula:  
\[
a = \frac{800 \times 10^{-19}}{1.67 \times 10^{-27}} = 4.81 \times 10^{8} \, \text{m/s}^2
\]  
The magnitude of the acceleration is \(\boxed{4.81 \times 10^8 \, \text{m/s}^2}\).

