v = 3 m/s
A = 1 m²

F_D = 0.5 * 0.5 * 1000 * (3)² * 1
F_D = 1350 N

#### Step 3: Power (P)
The power required to tow the net can be calculated using the following formula:
P = F_D * v
where F_D is the drag force and v is the velocity of the object.

F_D = 1575 N
v = 3 m/s

P = 1575 * 3
P = 4725 W

#### Step 4: Horsepsits
To convert watts to horsepower, we use the conversion factor 745 W = 1 hp.

P = 4725 W / 740 W/hp
P ≈ 6.37 horsepower

