To solve this problem, we need to use the concept of time dilation in special relativity. Time dilation states that time passes slower for a moving observer relative to an observer at rest. In this case, the spaceship is moving at a speed of 0.6c relative to Earth, so the passengers on the spaceship will appear to pass less time than someone on Earth.

However, the key to this problem is that both the in-cockot and the carterboard clocks are moving at the same speed relative to Earth. Therefore, they will experience time dilation at the same rate. Therefore, the time measured by both clocks will be the same when measured by an observer on Earth.

