We are given the standard Gibbs free energy of formation of water (H2O) as -237.1 kJ/mol. The standard Gibbs free energy of formation for a compound is the change in Gibbs free energy when 1 mole of the compound is formed from its elements in their standard states.

ΔG° = ΔG°(H2O) + ΔG°(O2) - 2ΔG°(H2)

