ΔG = ΔG° × n
where n is the number of moles of H2O produced. Since 2 moles of H2 and 1 mole of O2 react to produce 2 moles of H2O, we have:

n = 2 moles

ΔG = -474.2 kJ/mol × 2 moles = -948.4 kJ

