- Absorbed energy = 0.12 J  
- Mass of liver tissue = 1.6 kg  

First, convert the absorbed energy from J to mJ:  
\[
0.12 \text{ J} = 0.12 \times 10^6 \text{ mJ} = 120,000 \text{ mJ}
\]  
Next, convert the mass of liver tissue from kg to g:  
\[
1.6 \text{ kg} = 1.6 \times 1000 \text{ g} = 1600 \text{ g}
\]  
Now, substitute these values into the formula:  
\[
\text{dose (mSv)} = \frac{120,000 \text{ mJ}}{1600 \text{ g}} \times 10^{-6} \times 1000 = 75 \times 10^{-3} \text{ mSv} = 0.075 \text{ mSv}
\]  
