\]
The square of the four-momentum transfer \( Q^2 \) is then:
\[
Q^2 = q^2 = (q \cdot q) = \left( \frac{E_f - E_i}{c} \right)^2 + \left( \mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_i \right) \cdot \left( \mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_i \right).
\]
Simplifying the expression:
\[
Q^2 = \left( \frac{E_f - E_i}{c} \right)^2 + \left( \mathbf{p}_f \cdot \mathbf{p}_f - 2 \mathbf{p}_f \cdot \mathbf{p}_i + \mathbf{p}_i \cdot \mathbf{p}_i \right).
\]
Using the relativistic energy-momentum relation for the initial and final electrons:
\[
E_i^2 = (pc)^2 + m_e^2 \quad \text{and} \quad E_f^2 = (cp)^^2 + m_e^2.
\]
Substituting these into the expression for \( Q^2 \):
\[
